dsh-reasoning-adapter README · Troubleshooting：- `reports`: per model, the detected vendor, how it was detected (id / name / fuzzy / host), the levels and the compat fields added;
- `models`: the levels and default level DSH actually gives the picker;
- `match`: the write-back result. `wrote: true` means it wrote this time, `reason: "already matched"` means the config already agreed; any other `reason` explains a failure, in which case the runtime match still supplies the levels.
